.\" Manpage for gcat
.TH GCAT 1 "October 2023"
.SH NAME
gcat \- A command-line tool for fetching and displaying Gemini URLs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gcat
[\-q|--quiet]
[\-d|--debug]
[\-\-lenient]
[\-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.I url
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gcat
is a command-line utility that connects to Gemini servers to fetch and display content from Gemini URLs. It supports handling input requests, following redirects, and printing headers based on user preferences.
The response body is written to standard output as it arrives; a body that is not text is written as raw bytes.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quiet
Suppress the printing of header information.
.TP
.BR -d ", " --debug
Set logging level to INFO for debugging purposes.
.TP
.B --lenient
Don't fail on a text body that cannot be decoded.  If the charset is unknown,
assume UTF-8; if the body is not valid in its charset, replace the invalid
bytes.  A warning is printed to standard error in either case.  Without this
option such a body is an error (exit status 4).
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Give up after this many seconds and exit with status 99.  The default is 5.
The limit covers the whole operation, including any redirects, but not the
time spent waiting for the user to answer a prompt.
.TP
.I url
The Gemini URL to fetch. The URL should begin with "gemini://". If not specified, it will be prepended automatically.

.SH SIGNALS
.B gcat
handles the SIGALRM signal to implement a timeout mechanism, exiting with status code 99 if the operation takes longer than the timeout
(5 seconds unless changed with
.BR --timeout ).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B gcat gemini://example.com
Fetches and displays the content from the specified Gemini URL.

.TP
.B gcat -q gemini://example.com
Fetches the content from the specified URL without printing the header information.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.B gcat
exits with the following statuses:
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid URL or unsupported scheme.
.TP
.B 2
The server closed the connection without sending a TLS close_notify
alert, so the response may be truncated.  A warning is printed to
standard error; any data received is still printed.
.TP
.B 3
The server requested input, but standard input was at end of file.
.TP
.B 4
A text body could not be decoded: its charset is unknown, or it is not valid
in its charset.  Output up to the first invalid byte may already have been
written.  See
.BR --lenient .
.TP
.B 5
The server's response header was missing or malformed.
.TP
.B 99
Operation timed out (see
.BR --timeout ).

.SH NOTES
For debugging purposes, you can enable detailed logging by using the
.BR --debug
option. The utility will fetch the content using SSL with no hostname verification, which can be insecure.
.SH AUTHOR
Solderpunk
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR wget (1)
